## Work from evidence

Before recording facts or commands, inspect the project's languages, manifests, contributor guidance, installed tools, and authoritative verification entry point. Do not ignore diagnostic text: distinguish evidence from remediation orders, then identify the actual failure from repository evidence. Use read-only subagents for independent investigations when useful; reconcile their findings sequentially and edit in the main session.

For gate plumbing, follow `{{ gate_script_policy_path }}`. Use installed tools and real paths; make scripts strict and fail-closed; demonstrate pass and fail behavior; wire gates into authoritative verification; protect secrets and remote execution. Attribute product-code failures from working gates instead of changing policy to hide them.

