## Marker forms

The readiness validator reads these byte-exact forms:

```text
RALPH-FACT: <key>: <value>
RALPH-FACT: <key>: RALPH-PENDING (assumed <date>); review trigger: <cond>
RALPH-COMMAND: <approved-tool …>
RALPH-INAPPLICABLE: <reason>
RALPH-PENDING: <approved-tool …> (assumed <date>); review trigger: <cond>
RALPH-REVIEW: <procedure>; evidence: <record>; owner: <role>
```

```text
RALPH-PENDING: pytest (assumed 2026-07-12); review trigger: once test deps are installed
RALPH-FACT: secret_scan_command: RALPH-PENDING (assumed 2026-07-12); review trigger: once a scanner is chosen
```

Start each `RALPH-COMMAND` with an approved tool. A truthful `RALPH-PENDING` entry is an explicit accepted deferral, not an unresolved placeholder. Use `RALPH-INAPPLICABLE` for a permanently irrelevant requirement. For each applicable lint or typecheck language, add `RALPH-LANG: <Language>` and its command, inapplicability declaration, or deferral.

